{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md && git status --short && git diff --stat ddb770352f35f2f55c740e9a8479686de3a251e5..9e13fc96380396bfab2c5961c82dbcebad492550 && test -n \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" && printf '\"'review-cli-configured\\\\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md && git status --short && git diff --stat ddb770352f35f2f55c740e9a8479686de3a251e5..9e13fc96380396bfab2c5961c82dbcebad492550 && test -n \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" && printf '\"'review-cli-configured\\\\n'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: pose-review\ndescription: Use for POSE pull-request or code review to verify controlled scope, preserved contracts, security and observability impact, risk-proportional validation, and escalation where applicable. Trigger keywords - review, code review, PR review, review opinion, ultrareview.\nwhen_to_use: Evaluating your own or another author's diff or PR under POSE. Use before commenting or approving to select rules, inspect validation evidence and prior decisions, and issue an actionable decision.\npose_schema_range: \"1-1\"\nclients: agents-skills, mcp, claude-code\ncapabilities: read\n---\n\n# Skill: pose-review\n\n## Required reading\n\n1. [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md).\n2. [`.pose/workflows/review.md`](../../../.pose/workflows/review.md).\n3. Applicable domain rules; security takes precedence in conflicts.\n\nResolve the selected task with `pose context --task <typed-or-qualified-artifact-ref> --json` before reviewing. Follow its canonical authority and stop on ambiguity, stale binding, unsupported metadata or `transfer-in-progress`. Use the qualified `xref:` scope for cross-project review; every cross-project write requires an explicit `POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS` binding and the current `context_revision` as `--expect-context`. Keep review evidence and its `POSE-Spec:` trailer in the authority repository.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Classify the change as feature, bugfix, refactor, documentation, or mixed.\n2. Run `pose assess tech-debt` during code review to ensure markers (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `stub`, `panic`) are covered by follow-ups or specs. Run `pose assess integrate` when touching inter-module contracts (Protobuf, Kafka, REST, MCP).\n3. Resolve `pose review bundle <scope> --explain` to inspect effective criteria, components and tool requirements.\n4. Run active required tools first, record why each recommended tool was used or skipped, and keep completion tools deferred until attestation.\n5. Select rules with `pose suggest review --path <affected-dir>` for every mapped component.\n6. Search `.pose/knowledge/` for prior module decisions, accepted risks, and pending follow-ups.\n7. Require deterministic `pose validate --strict` evidence matching delivery targets.\n8. Evaluate every required plan criterion, including cross-component boundaries. When the change adds or alters a governance gate, also answer: what is the cheapest way to satisfy this gate in form without producing its value, and what stops that? Point to the adversarial corpus case that proves it (`pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md`), or record the gap.\n9. Classify findings as critical, high, medium, or low with evidence and expected action.\n10. Run `pose recurrence-check --tolerant --window-days 14`; use recurrence escalation for a matching systemic signal.\n11. Create a handoff with `pose new-knowledge handoff <slug>` for accepted residual risk, monitoring, or deferred action.\n12. Seal the review subject with `pose review bundle <scope> --seal`.\n13. Prepare the mechanical half with `pose review auto-attest <bundle-id> --reviewer agent:<id>` — without `--apply` — and read `review_attestation.pending`: those are the criteria no registered check answers, and they are yours to answer. Then record the attestation with `pose review attest`, giving every judgment criterion a conclusion. `--apply` on auto-attest records only when nothing is pending; it refuses otherwise, and never answers a judgment criterion for you. An explicit attestation records `--criterion ID|passed|evidence` (or `not-applicable` with a rationale, or `finding` naming a recorded finding) and `--finding ID|severity|disposition|action|evidence[|owner|rationale|review-by]`; every finding needs a severity and an action, and an `accepted-risk` or `wont-fix` finding also needs an owner, a rationale and a review date. A `passed` criterion may cite only evidence the sealed bundle contains, of a class the criterion accepts. For a cross-project attestation, use the qualified `xref:` as the target argument to `pose review attest`, include `--expect-context <digest>` with `--apply`, and keep the explicit project binding; a bundle ID alone does not select an authority project.\n14. Run `pose review verify <scope>` and `pose review-check <scope>`; close only when both confirm a valid, approved attestation.\n15. Decide: approved, approved with reservations, changes requested, or rejected.\n16. When Contributor Mode is active, if review uncovers POSE linter false-positives, diagnostic frictions, or rule gaps, stage an improvement proposal with `pose contribute stage --type enhancement --title \"<summary>\"`.\n\n## Output requirements\n\n- Completed Rules applied during review section.\n- Bundle/plan digests and dispositions for required, recommended and deferred completion tools.\n- Severity-classified findings with expected actions.\n- Clear and actionable final decision.\n- Handoff when residual risk is accepted.\n .pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json              | 3951 ++++++++++++++------\n .pose/indexes/generation.json                      |   18 +-\n .pose/indexes/spec-graph.json                      | 1228 +++---\n .pose/policy/delegation.json                       |   22 +-\n .pose/results/assess-sealed-binding.md             |    2 +\n .pose/results/delivery-validation.json             | 1322 +++----\n .pose/results/reap-binding.md                      |   16 +\n .../0bb5cb993d1f7d42b4be131a/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../0bb5cb993d1f7d42b4be131a/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../13be3e0d9eb721a49795feab/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../13be3e0d9eb721a49795feab/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../13be3e0d9eb721a49795feab/000002.json           |   12 +\n .../13be3e0d9eb721a49795feab/000002.result.json    |    6 +\n .../24c92f0f02b9cd31fee83a86/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../24c92f0f02b9cd31fee83a86/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../362d76c2217cf80193435863/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../362d76c2217cf80193435863/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../39383823d22951ef02e66d51/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../39383823d22951ef02e66d51/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../3dbcfb3383e26c36d9402812/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../3dbcfb3383e26c36d9402812/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../45a7f7f91f18049364f42b7c/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../45a7f7f91f18049364f42b7c/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../529e6fdc431afa130d108259/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../529e6fdc431afa130d108259/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../649a3bf257ce8f047ce6bcae/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../649a3bf257ce8f047ce6bcae/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../968095248fe66e9917d89286/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../968095248fe66e9917d89286/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../adb171ce4f406c3546505bc0/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../adb171ce4f406c3546505bc0/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../b403109df35cbe70b9714ad5/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../b403109df35cbe70b9714ad5/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../cf147e02b9122d5096b97653/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../cf147e02b9122d5096b97653/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../e77c0116a3eeab9b1da7488e/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../e77c0116a3eeab9b1da7488e/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../eda71804dc51badccc553dea/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../eda71804dc51badccc553dea/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../f098a3d45ce5bb8d81209dfa/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../f098a3d45ce5bb8d81209dfa/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../f098a3d45ce5bb8d81209dfa/000002.json           |   12 +\n .../f098a3d45ce5bb8d81209dfa/000002.result.json