{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' .pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go | sed -n '130,205p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '86,140p'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\nstatus: draft        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\ncreated_at: 2026-11-25\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on: pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority: 3\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: feature\nsurface: standard\ndelivers:            # optional typed refs: surface:id, contract:id, capability:id, infrastructure:id, governance:id\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nCarry the guarantees `pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes` gives on Linux (through the review run shim) and on Windows (through a job object) to the remaining cases: other Unix platforms, the identities of what Windows and Unix group kills ended, and the environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim.\n\n### Business value\nReview rounds 13 and 14 of that spec found these gaps; by the maintainer's decision on 2026-11-25 they were moved here so that spec could close on its declared scope (Linux and Windows termination).\n\n### Constraints\nNo new guarantee is claimed before it is enforced and tested on the platform it names.\n\n### Non-goals\nChanging the Linux shim or the Windows job object.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: On Unix platforms other than Linux, after the process-group kill the dispatch shall wait, within a bound, until the group is proven empty, and leave the cleanup incomplete otherwise (round 14, N2).\n- R2: When the Windows job object or a Unix group kill ends processes, the run record shall name them, as the Linux shim's report does (round 14, N3).\n- R3: The environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim shall not end a process it cannot prove belongs to the run, for example by constraining it to the run's descendants (round 14, N1; limit L6 of the parent spec).\n- R4: Each requirement shall have a test on the platform it concerns, run in CI where that platform is available.\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp` review dispatch, its platform files and the manual.\n\n### Artifacts\nDeclared when the spec starts.\n\n### Delivery targets\nDeclared when the spec starts.\n\n### API/contract changes\nTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n\n### Technical risks\nTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [ ] Confirm CI availability for macOS and Windows before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test on its platform.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n\n### Results summary\n\n### Requirement trace\n\n### Known gaps\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\n### Files and modules changed\n\n### Validation executed\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n   130\t\t}\n   131\t\tfor {\n   132\t\t\tchildren := 0\n   133\t\t\tproblems = problems[:0]\n   134\t\t\t// /proc is read in batches under the deadline, never materialized\n   135\t\t\t// whole (review round 13, N3).\n   136\t\t\tdirs, err := readProcBatched(deadline)\n   137\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   138\t\t\t\tnote(err)\n   139\t\t\t}\n   140\t\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n   141\t\t\t\t// The bound holds per process, not only per listing (review round\n   142\t\t\t\t// 14, N4).\n   143\t\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n   144\t\t\t\t\tchildren++\n   145\t\t\t\t\tnote(fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be scanned within the bound\"))\n   146\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   147\t\t\t\t}\n   148\t\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n   149\t\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n   150\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   151\t\t\t\t}\n   152\t\t\t\tst, err := readShimProcStat(pid)\n   153\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) {\n   154\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   155\t\t\t\t}\n   156\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   157\t\t\t\t\t// A process of another user is never the run's: with procfs\n   158\t\t\t\t\t// mounted hidepid it is visible and unreadable (review round 10,\n   159\t\t\t\t\t// N1). Only one of this user is an unknown that may be the run's.\n   160\t\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) || oerr == nil && owner != os.Getuid() {\n   161\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   162\t\t\t\t\t}\n   163\t\t\t\t\tchildren++\n   164\t\t\t\t\tnote(fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err))\n   165\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   166\t\t\t\t}\n   167\t\t\t\tif st.ppid != self {\n   168\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   169\t\t\t\t}\n   170\t\t\t\tchildren++\n   171\t\t\t\tif !st.zombie {\n   172\t\t\t\t\t// A pid is reported ended only once its signal was delivered\n   173\t\t\t\t\t// (review round 10, N3).\n   174\t\t\t\t\tif delivered, err := killPinnedChild(pid, self); err != nil {\n   175\t\t\t\t\t\tnote(err)\n   176\t\t\t\t\t} else if delivered {\n   177\t\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n   178\t\t\t\t\t}\n   179\t\t\t\t}\n   180\t\t\t}\n   181\t\t\tfor {\n   182\t\t\t\tpid, err := unix.Wait4(-1, nil, unix.WNOHANG, nil)\n   183\t\t\t\tif pid <= 0 || err != nil {\n   184\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   185\t\t\t\t}\n   186\t\t\t\t// A pid is reported ended once it was signalled and reaped\n   187\t\t\t\t// (review round 12, N2).\n   188\t\t\t\tif seen[pid] {\n   189\t\t\t\t\tdelete(seen, pid)\n   190\t\t\t\t\tended = append(ended, strconv.Itoa(pid))\n   191\t\t\t\t}\n   192\t\t\t}\n   193\t\t\tif children == 0 && len(problems) == 0 {\n   194\t\t\t\treturn ended, nil\n   195\t\t\t}\n   196\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n   197\t\t\t\treturn ended, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended: %s\", children, strings.Join(problems, \"; \"))\n   198\t\t\t}\n   199\t\t\ttime.Sleep(20 * time.Millisecond)\n   200\t\t}\n   201\t}\n   202\t\n   203\ttype shimProcStat struct {\n   204\t\tppid   int\n   205\t\tzombie bool\n    86\t// reviewMarkedProcesses lists the live processes whose environment holds\n    87\t// entry, and counts this user's processes whose environment could not be\n    88\t// read. A process that is gone is skipped.\n    89\tfunc reviewMarkedProcesses(entry []byte, deadline time.Time) ([]int, map[int]string, error) {\n    90\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n    91\t\tif err != nil {\n    92\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    93\t\t}\n    94\t\tunreadable := map[int]string{}\n    95\t\tself, uid := os.Getpid(), os.Getuid()\n    96\t\tvar out []int\n    97\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n    98\t\t\tif !deadline.IsZero() && time.Now().After(deadline) {\n    99\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be scanned within the bound\")\n   100\t\t\t}\n   101\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n   102\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n   103\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   104\t\t\t}\n   105\t\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   106\t\t\tswitch {\n   107\t\t\tcase reviewProcessGoneErr(err):\n   108\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   109\t\t\tcase err != nil:\n   110\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); oerr == nil && owner != uid {\n   111\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // another user's process never inherits this run's environment\n   112\t\t\t\t} else if reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) {\n   113\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   114\t\t\t\t}\n   115\t\t\t\tstart, serr := processStartTime(pid)\n   116\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(serr) {\n   117\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   118\t\t\t\t}\n   119\t\t\t\tif serr != nil || start == \"\" {\n   120\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d start could not be read: %v\", pid, serr)\n   121\t\t\t\t}\n   122\t\t\t\tunreadable[pid] = start\n   123\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   124\t\t\tcase !marked:\n   125\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   126\t\t\t}\n   127\t\t\tzombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid)\n   128\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && zombie {\n   129\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   130\t\t\t}\n   131\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   132\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state could not be read: %w\", pid, err)\n   133\t\t\t}\n   134\t\t\tout = append(out, pid)\n   135\t\t}\n   136\t\treturn out, unreadable, nil\n   137\t}\n   138\t\n   139\t// killPinnedMarkedProcess signals pid only through a pidfd opened on it,\n   140\t// after the environment read through that same pinned process still holds\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
