{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '172,205p' .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '172,205p' .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n### Known gaps\nThe release is driven through the Store, including after a real interrupted dispatch; the thin `pose delegate cancel` branch that calls it is not driven through the CLI, because a stalled marker there needs a dispatch process killed and three silent heartbeat intervals. N5 (the receipt inspection error) has no test: making the receipt path uninspectable also makes the reservation unreadable first.\n\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe dispatch ends the processes a run left running before its cleanup and names them in the run record; `pose delegate cancel` releases an attempt abandoned before its run was recorded; `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish.\n\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` (review dispatch, attempt ledger, delegation CLI, brief), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies.\n\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n\n### Residual risks\nL1: on Linux a run's process escapes only while it keeps a live parent outside the run and neither the run's group nor its environment entry, for example one handed to a service manager; the cleanup inventory still fails a run whose files it keeps changing. L2: on other Unix platforms only the process-group kill applies. On Windows the adapter runs in a kill-on-close job object; its test (`TestTheReviewersJobEndsItsDescendants`) is built for Windows and was compiled and vetted here, but not run, since this host is Linux. L6: an embedder that does not enable the shim falls back to the search by the sealed-checkout entry, which a reviewer process can set. L4: a reservation an earlier engine left without a marker records no owner, so its release rests on the operator's confirmation, not on proof. L3: a process of this user that made itself non-inspectable cannot be matched: one that predates the run is skipped and counted in the run record, and one started during the run fails the cleanup, so such a run is not concludable.\n\n\n### Follow-ups\nCarried by `pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux`: group emptiness on other Unix, naming what Windows and Unix group kills ended, and the embedder fallback (L6).\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
