{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md | sed -n '1,58p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go | sed -n '240,300p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go | sed -n '980,1002p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tslug: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\n     3\tstatus: draft        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n     4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-25\n     5\tcompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\n     6\tsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\n     7\tdepends_on: pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\n     8\tremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\n     9\tpriority: 3\n    10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n    11\ttask_type: feature\n    12\tsurface: standard\n    13\tdelivers:            # optional typed refs: surface:id, contract:id, capability:id, infrastructure:id, governance:id\n    14\t---\n    15\t\n    16\t# Spec: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\n    17\t\n    18\t## 1. Intent\n    19\t\n    20\t### Goal\n    21\tCarry the guarantees `pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes` gives on Linux (through the review run shim) and on Windows (through a job object) to the remaining cases: other Unix platforms, the identities of what Windows and Unix group kills ended, and the environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim.\n    22\t\n    23\t### Business value\n    24\tReview rounds 13 and 14 of that spec found these gaps; by the maintainer's decision on 2026-11-25 they were moved here so that spec could close on its declared scope (Linux and Windows termination).\n    25\t\n    26\t### Constraints\n    27\tNo new guarantee is claimed before it is enforced and tested on the platform it names.\n    28\t\n    29\t### Non-goals\n    30\tChanging the Linux shim or the Windows job object.\n    31\t\n    32\t## 2. Requirements\n    33\t\n    34\t### Functional\n    35\t- R1: On Unix platforms other than Linux, after the process-group kill the dispatch shall wait, within a bound, until the group is proven empty, and leave the cleanup incomplete otherwise (round 14, N2).\n    36\t- R2: When the Windows job object or a Unix group kill ends processes, the run record shall name them, as the Linux shim's report does (round 14, N3).\n    37\t- R3: The environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim shall not end a process it cannot prove belongs to the run, for example by constraining it to the run's descendants (round 14, N1; limit L6 of the parent spec).\n    38\t- R4: Each requirement shall have a test on the platform it concerns, run in CI where that platform is available.\n    39\t\n    40\t### Non-functional\n    41\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n    42\t\n    43\t### Security\n    44\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n    45\t\n    46\t### Compatibility\n    47\tRecords written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n    48\t\n    49\t## 3. Technical Plan\n    50\t\n    51\t### Affected areas\n    52\t`pose-mcp` review dispatch, its platform files and the manual.\n    53\t\n    54\t### Artifacts\n    55\tDeclared when the spec starts.\n    56\t\n    57\t### Delivery targets\n    58\tDeclared when the spec starts.\n   240\t\t// A recorded run does not finish an attempt, its receipt does: a\n   241\t\t// reservation whose run was recorded without a receipt still blocks and\n   242\t\t// is released with that run (review round 5, N3).\n   243\t\t_ = runs\n   244\t\tvar out []DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   245\t\tvar lost []string\n   246\t\tbudget := reviewReadBudget(nil)\n   247\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n   248\t\t\tif !d.IsDir() {\n   249\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   250\t\t\t}\n   251\t\t\tentries, truncated, err := readDirBounded(filepath.Join(base, d.Name()), reviewOrphanScanMaxEntries)\n   252\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   253\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the reservations in \"+d.Name()+\" could not be listed: \"+err.Error())\n   254\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   255\t\t\t}\n   256\t\t\tif truncated {\n   257\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, fmt.Sprintf(\"the reservations in %s exceed %d entries; the rest were not read\", d.Name(), reviewOrphanScanMaxEntries))\n   258\t\t\t}\n   259\t\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n   260\t\t\t\tif IsPublisherStaging(e.Name()) || !strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".json\") || strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".result.json\") {\n   261\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   262\t\t\t\t}\n   263\t\t\t\tvar a DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   264\t\t\t\tif err := readLedgerJSONBudgetIn(s.fsys(), filepath.Join(base, d.Name(), e.Name()), &a, budget); err != nil {\n   265\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the reservation \"+d.Name()+\"/\"+e.Name()+\" could not be read: \"+err.Error())\n   266\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   267\t\t\t\t}\n   268\t\t\t\tif a.AttemptID != attemptIdentity(a) {\n   269\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the reservation \"+d.Name()+\"/\"+e.Name()+\" does not match its identity\")\n   270\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   271\t\t\t\t}\n   272\t\t\t\tif marked[a.AttemptID] {\n   273\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   274\t\t\t\t}\n   275\t\t\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, a)); err == nil {\n   276\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   277\t\t\t\t} else if !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   278\t\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the receipt of \"+a.AttemptID+\" could not be inspected: \"+err.Error())\n   279\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   280\t\t\t\t}\n   281\t\t\t\tat, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, a.ReservedAt)\n   282\t\t\t\tif err != nil || now.Sub(at) < reviewOrphanReservationAge {\n   283\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   284\t\t\t\t}\n   285\t\t\t\tout = append(out, a)\n   286\t\t\t}\n   287\t\t}\n   288\t\tif dirsTruncated {\n   289\t\t\tlost = append(lost, fmt.Sprintf(\"the attempt directories exceed %d entries; the rest were not read\", reviewOrphanScanMaxEntries))\n   290\t\t}\n   291\t\t// Without the whole run history nothing is known to have no run, except\n   292\t\t// the loss of an orphan's own abandonment run an interrupted release left\n   293\t\t// before its record (review round 14, N5).\n   294\t\tfor _, a := range out {\n   295\t\t\town, _ := identifiedReviewRun(abandonmentRun(a, nil), nil)\n   296\t\t\trunLost = withoutOwnWitness(runLost, own.RunID)\n   297\t\t}\n   298\t\tif len(runLost) > 0 {\n   299\t\t\treturn nil, append([]string{\"abandoned reservations cannot be determined while the run history is incomplete\"}, runLost...), nil\n   300\t\t}\n   980\t\t\tself, err := os.Executable()\n   981\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   982\t\t\t\treturn finish(ReviewRunFailed, \"the review run shim could not be set up: \"+err.Error())\n   983\t\t\t}\n   984\t\t\tr, w, err := os.Pipe()\n   985\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   986\t\t\t\treturn finish(ReviewRunFailed, \"the review run shim could not be set up: \"+err.Error())\n   987\t\t\t}\n   988\t\t\tuseShim, shimRead, shimWrite = true, r, w\n   989\t\t\tcmd = exec.CommandContext(ctx, self, append([]string{ReviewShimArg, cmd.Path}, argv...)...)\n   990\t\t\tcmd.ExtraFiles = []*os.File{w}\n   991\t\t}\n   992\t\tcmd.Dir = worktree\n   993\t\tcmd.Stdin = strings.NewReader(plan.Brief.Text)\n   994\t\tenv, secrets, err := reviewAdapterEnvironment(plan.Config, tmp, plan.Brief.Text, plan.notes)\n   995\t\tif err != nil {\n   996\t\t\trun.BriefNotes = \"\"\n   997\t\t\treturn finish(ReviewRunFailed, err.Error())\n   998\t\t}\n   999\t\tunset := []string{}\n  1000\t\tif policy, _, found, perr := s.LoadDelegationPolicy(); perr == nil && found {\n  1001\t\t\tunset = policy.EnvUnset\n  1002\t\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"The targeted Linux dispatch and release tests, the interrupted-witness recovery test, and `go vet` pass. The two strict validation commands could not create Go build directories in this read-only checkout; the sealed bundle has passing build, unit, integration, and e2e evidence. The source review found two low-severity edge cases in the release/list path and shim setup error handling; I’m including them as owned follow-ups and will validate the exact draft next."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_REVIEW_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\nReview summary: approved with two low-severity follow-ups accepted for the next maintenance window. N1: a markerless reservation is silently omitted from the listing when any receipt file exists, even if that receipt is unreadable. N2: the Linux report pipe is not closed when adapter-environment validation fails before launch. The focused dispatch/release tests, interrupted-witness recovery test, and go vet passed. Strict validate commands were attempted but Go could not create build directories in the read-only sandbox; sealed build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence passes. The Windows runtime test was not run on this Linux host, as recorded in L2.\n\ndecision: approved\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 275,\n      \"summary\": \"The orphan scan treats any existing receipt path as a completed attempt without reading or validating the receipt. A corrupt receipt makes delegate ls omit the reservation while later dispatch admission rejects it, leaving a blocked attempt without a loss entry.\",\n      \"action\": \"Validate and bind an existing receipt before omitting its reservation; report unreadable receipts as losses and keep the attempt visible.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 997,\n      \"summary\": \"After opening the Linux shim report pipe, an adapter-environment validation error returns without closing either pipe end. Repeated failed dispatches in a long-lived embedder can retain descriptors until garbage collection.\",\n      \"action\": \"Close both report-pipe ends on every pre-launch error path and add a repeated validation-failure descriptor-count regression test.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-25\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"superseded\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md:20-24,37\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"superseded\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md:35,38\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"superseded\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md:36,38\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:134-145; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:97-100\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N5\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run '\"'\"'^TestAReleaseInterruptedAfterTheWitnessCompletes$'\"' -count=1 passed; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:509-539\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the Linux shim and process reaper, dispatch lifecycle and run records, Windows job-object path, non-Linux stubs, reservation/release/list/cancel and round accounting, the review brief and manual/scaffold mirrors, and the regression tests. Checked transferred non-Linux and embedder-fallback concerns against pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.\\\"\n  ,\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified that the Linux CLI re-enters the same executable as an isolated subreaper and that Windows assigns the suspended adapter to a kill-on-close job before resuming it. L2 records that the Windows runtime test was not run on this Linux host; other Unix behavior and the embedder fallback are explicitly carried to the follow-up spec. The remaining Linux escape case in L1 is stated as a residual risk.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The report pipe is opened before environment validation and the error return does not close it.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change adds the cancel release behavior and brief template version while retaining the run/receipt schema. The Linux CLI process-tree path is covered by the dispatch test; the CLI cancel route itself remains a documented test gap.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An unreadable or malformed receipt is treated as proof of completion in the orphan listing, so the attempt is omitted even though admission later rejects it.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed path stays within pose-mcp delegation and review-run lifecycle handling; no HTTP, event, protobuf, or MCP contract is changed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The invalid-receipt case does not appear in delegate ls losses, so the blocked attempt is not diagnosable from the listing.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new failed run is recorded with the existing run and receipt formats. The old-engine meaning remains an ordinary failed run; markerless older reservations require explicit operator confirmation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The core Linux process cleanup and deterministic release recovery are correct under the tested cases; the corrupt-receipt path can still leave a reservation blocking dispatch without a visible loss.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the ownership cause with a child-only subreaper shim, avoiding the dispatcher's process-wide subreaper and reviewer-controlled environment matching on the standard Linux path. D2 closes abandoned attempts with a deterministic failed-run record and receipt rather than deleting the reservation. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The English, Portuguese, and scaffold manuals describe Linux shim, Windows job-object, other-Unix, and embedder-fallback behavior; review-brief/10 asks commands to finish.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The invalid-receipt state lacks a loss message and actionable listing row, although the normal abandoned-release path reports the failed run and status.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R5's normal no-receipt interruption path is covered by release and next-dispatch tests, but an existing unreadable receipt can hide a reservation that still blocks a later dispatch.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation delivers R1-R6 and D1-D2. The additional beyond-Linux spec tracks the explicitly transferred platform and embedder cases.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux path uses process ancestry rather than reviewer-settable environment ownership, the report pipe is not inherited by the adapter, PIDs are pinned before signals, and the Windows adapter is suspended until assigned to its job. L6 remains an explicit embedder limitation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A process-group kill misses setsid descendants, environment matching is not trustworthy for the standard CLI, and putting a subreaper in the dispatcher would affect unrelated work. The shim and suspended Windows job are the smallest isolated ownership mechanisms for the declared platforms. A live process handed outside the run can invalidate the Linux guarantee as L1 states.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exited 0. It reported 35 claims and 41 observed paths with repository-wide orphan warnings; its change-set head differed from the sealed bundle subject, so those totals are treated as a provenance caveat.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended design assessment; it observed zero deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended assessment. It reported no consumers observed for /admin/refresh, /healthz, and /mcp; these are repository-wide observations outside the changed review-dispatch and CLI-cancel boundaries.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs were invalid, and it reported one uncovered debt marker; changed subject files contain no TODO or FIXME markers.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check requires a recorded attestation, which this review brief forbids recording.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check requires the review attestation to exist; the brief requires it remain unrecorded.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The strict surface check completed with one target and zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The command was attempted but the sandbox prevented Go from creating build directories. The sealed bundle contains passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and vet also passed locally.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The module command was attempted but stopped because the checkout and Go cache are read-only. The sealed module evidence covers the validation matrix; focused regression tests and go vet passed.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_REVIEW_FINAL\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_REVIEW_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\nReview summary: approved with two low-severity follow-ups accepted for the next maintenance window. N1: a markerless reservation is silently omitted from the listing when any receipt file exists, even if that receipt is unreadable. N2: the Linux report pipe is not closed when adapter-environment validation fails before launch. The focused dispatch/release tests, interrupted-witness recovery test, and go vet passed. Strict validate commands were attempted but Go could not create build directories in the read-only sandbox; sealed build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence passes. The Windows runtime test was not run on this Linux host, as recorded in L2.\n\ndecision: approved\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 275,\n      \"summary\": \"The orphan scan treats any existing receipt path as a completed attempt without reading or validating the receipt. A corrupt receipt makes delegate ls omit the reservation while later dispatch admission rejects it, leaving a blocked attempt without a loss entry.\",\n      \"action\": \"Validate and bind an existing receipt before omitting its reservation; report unreadable receipts as losses and keep the attempt visible.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 997,\n      \"summary\": \"After opening the Linux shim report pipe, an adapter-environment validation error returns without closing either pipe end. Repeated failed dispatches in a long-lived embedder can retain descriptors until garbage collection.\",\n      \"action\": \"Close both report-pipe ends on every pre-launch error path and add a repeated validation-failure descriptor-count regression test.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-25\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"superseded\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md:20-24,37\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"superseded\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md:35,38\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"superseded\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md:36,38\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:134-145; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:97-100\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N5\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run '\"'\"'^TestAReleaseInterruptedAfterTheWitnessCompletes$'\"' -count=1 passed; pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:509-539\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the Linux shim and process reaper, dispatch lifecycle and run records, Windows job-object path, non-Linux stubs, reservation/release/list/cancel and round accounting, the review brief and manual/scaffold mirrors, and the regression tests. Checked transferred non-Linux and embedder-fallback concerns against pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.\\\"\n  ,\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified that the Linux CLI re-enters the same executable as an isolated subreaper and that Windows assigns the suspended adapter to a kill-on-close job before resuming it. L2 records that the Windows runtime test was not run on this Linux host; other Unix behavior and the embedder fallback are explicitly carried to the follow-up spec. The remaining Linux escape case in L1 is stated as a residual risk.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The report pipe is opened before environment validation and the error return does not close it.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change adds the cancel release behavior and brief template version while retaining the run/receipt schema. The Linux CLI process-tree path is covered by the dispatch test; the CLI cancel route itself remains a documented test gap.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An unreadable or malformed receipt is treated as proof of completion in the orphan listing, so the attempt is omitted even though admission later rejects it.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-marker-stop-joins-heartbeat-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed path stays within pose-mcp delegation and review-run lifecycle handling; no HTTP, event, protobuf, or MCP contract is changed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The invalid-receipt case does not appear in delegate ls losses, so the blocked attempt is not diagnosable from the listing.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new failed run is recorded with the existing run and receipt formats. The old-engine meaning remains an ordinary failed run; markerless older reservations require explicit operator confirmation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The core Linux process cleanup and deterministic release recovery are correct under the tested cases; the corrupt-receipt path can still leave a reservation blocking dispatch without a visible loss.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the ownership cause with a child-only subreaper shim, avoiding the dispatcher's process-wide subreaper and reviewer-controlled environment matching on the standard Linux path. D2 closes abandoned attempts with a deterministic failed-run record and receipt rather than deleting the reservation. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The English, Portuguese, and scaffold manuals describe Linux shim, Windows job-object, other-Unix, and embedder-fallback behavior; review-brief/10 asks commands to finish.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The invalid-receipt state lacks a loss message and actionable listing row, although the normal abandoned-release path reports the failed run and status.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R5's normal no-receipt interruption path is covered by release and next-dispatch tests, but an existing unreadable receipt can hide a reservation that still blocks a later dispatch.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation delivers R1-R6 and D1-D2. The additional beyond-Linux spec tracks the explicitly transferred platform and embedder cases.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux path uses process ancestry rather than reviewer-settable environment ownership, the report pipe is not inherited by the adapter, PIDs are pinned before signals, and the Windows adapter is suspended until assigned to its job. L6 remains an explicit embedder limitation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A process-group kill misses setsid descendants, environment matching is not trustworthy for the standard CLI, and putting a subreaper in the dispatcher would affect unrelated work. The shim and suspended Windows job are the smallest isolated ownership mechanisms for the declared platforms. A live process handed outside the run can invalidate the Linux guarantee as L1 states.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exited 0. It reported 35 claims and 41 observed paths with repository-wide orphan warnings; its change-set head differed from the sealed bundle subject, so those totals are treated as a provenance caveat.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-d8fb4eee1d869659\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended design assessment; it observed zero deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended assessment. It reported no consumers observed for /admin/refresh, /healthz, and /mcp; these are repository-wide observations outside the changed review-dispatch and CLI-cancel boundaries.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs were invalid, and it reported one uncovered debt marker; changed subject files contain no TODO or FIXME markers.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check requires a recorded attestation, which this review brief forbids recording.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check requires the review attestation to exist; the brief requires it remain unrecorded.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The strict surface check completed with one target and zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The command was attempted but the sandbox prevented Go from creating build directories. The sealed bundle contains passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and vet also passed locally.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The module command was attempted but stopped because the checkout and Go cache are read-only. The sealed module evidence covers the validation matrix; focused regression tests and go vet passed.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_REVIEW_FINAL\n'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would refuse this draft:\n  - the draft does not account for its round: prior finding R13-N2 is not accounted for; prior finding R13-N3 is not accounted for\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
